From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 04:54:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] feat(registry): record resource changes for controllers

Nothing in the control plane could find out that a resource had been
created, updated or deleted, so no controller could react to API writes.

Append a row to a new resource_changes table in the same transaction as
every resources write (created, updated, terminating, deleted). Consumers
read it incrementally with changes_since(seq) and clean up with
prune_changes(seq); seq is AUTOINCREMENT so it is never reused after
pruning. list_resource_keys() lists resource keys across tenants so a
controller can rebuild its work queue on startup. Both cross-tenant reads
are for the control plane itself and must not be exposed through the API.
